s Teach For Us Membership Options Join Or Renew Membership Upcoming Trips Corporate Sponsor & Memberships For Current Members Meet Our Staff LRU4U Youth Programs Adult Fitness Programs Community Programs Indoor Pool Rental NextStep@LRU Contact Our Staff About About Leadership Inauguration Our Neighborhood Map, Directions & Parking Employment Opportunities Staff Openings Faculty Openings Event Rental Space Confrencing Indoor Pool Rental Wedding Ceremony Rentals Public Safety Hazing Policy Vehicle Immobilization & Towing Policy Accreditations Ask Questions Contact Us Home » Adjunct Clinical Instructor – Mental Health Nursing Adjunct Clinical Instructor – Mental Health Nursing La Roche University is seeking qualified candidates for an Adjunct Clinical Instructor position in Mental Health Nursing for our innovative Direct Entry Master of Science in Nursing (DEMSN) program—the first such program in Pennsylvania. La Roche University continues to enhance and expand its health programs while embracing its Catholic identity and welcoming people of all faiths and backgrounds. We foster global citizenship and create a community of scholars dedicated to promoting justice and peace in our constantly changing global society. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: Direct, manage, and evaluate student learning during mental health clinical experiences at local healthcare facilities and the University’s Clinical Simulation Center Facilitate the development of therapeutic communication, psychiatric assessment skills, and clinical reasoning in various mental health settings Guide students in providing compassionate, evidence-based care to individuals with mental health conditions Assist students in integrating psychiatric-mental health theory with clinical practice, specific to course learning outcomes Collaborate with course instructors on student learning activities, progress, and concerns Support students in developing cultural competence and reducing stigma in mental health care Education/Qualifications: Current Pennsylvania RN license and Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) required Minimum of 2 years psychiatric/mental health nursing experience required Clinical teaching experience preferred Strong interpersonal and communication skills Ability to work both independently and as part of a team Experience with mental health simulation scenarios a plus Candidates must pass background clearances and submit official transcripts prior to the issuance of a contract. Review of applicants will begin immediately; position open until filled. Applicants must reside and work from one of the following states : PA, WV, VA, DE, NJ, MD, FL; or DC. Applicants who reside in OH must work on site at our PA campus. Qualified applicants can complete an online application by clicking on the following link. Your application will not be considered unless you include a letter of interest, resume/CV, and a list of professional references. CLICK HERE TO APPLY This is considered an adjunct faculty position. Adjunct faculty are hired for specific teaching assignments and contracts are distributed on a semester-by-semester basis with no guarantee of future contracts. Applicants for this position must have current legal authorization to work in the United States. La Roche University will not sponsor or take over the sponsorship of an employment visa for this opportunity. It is the policy of La Roche University to promote equal opportunity to all qualified individuals regardless of race, color creed, age, religion, gender, national or ethnic origin, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, non-job-related disability or medical condition, or any other legally protected status. How to Apply You must submit a separate online application for each position that you want to apply for. The positions listed on this site are those currently available at the University. The information listed for each position is all that is available at this time. There is no further need to contact the Human Re"
    },
